  // (highest priority -- the render was refused, so this supersedes the
  // staleness/root warnings) and the user learns the allowed combinations by
  // doing. Cleared to '' on any successful render reply. Empty-window (a
  // VALID answer, success:true) is tracked separately (dockedSinceEmptyWindow)
  // and shown as an informational note, NOT an error.
  let dockedServerSinceError = '';
  let dockedSinceEmptyWindow = false;
  // ISSUE-2 GUARD (Dan, 2026-06-22): the uuid of the row for which the bottom
  // render pane currently holds GOOD (successfully-composed) content. Set by
  // applyDockedServerMarkdown on success; CLEARED at every selection change /
  // root re-set (in setDockedSelection / prepareDockedServerRender) so the
  // leave-previous-content-to-avoid-a-flash window does NOT count as good
  // content for the NEW row. A late / timed-out / null server reply for the
  // row we are ALREADY viewing must NOT wipe a good render with the server-
  // unavailable error; but a genuinely new selection (or a Refresh) with a
  // down socket SHOULD show the error. Keying on do-we-already-have-good-
