      // — symptoms #4/#5). Instead we enter FROZEN-DOM-SINGLE mode: CAPTURE the
      // current visible tree into a stable in-memory tree and route each frozen
      // row click through the EXISTING single-render path against THAT captured
      // tree (one ~0.5s render per clicked row; DOM mutation after freeze is
      // irrelevant because the tree is cached). Freeze is now INSTANT.
      //
