  //   kind=ast,
  //   comment=Feature 2 dock affordance ('GLIMPSE what the modal is showing right now'): copy the FULL render_spec blob (scope + selected-row focus) as compact JSON to the clipboard, so the human hands it to an agent verbatim as workflowy_glimpse(render_spec=<blob>) to render EXACTLY this row's option-Y view server-side. Uses the SAME currentDockRenderSpecWithSelectedFocus() helper as the render_spec='modal' WS leaf query, preventing copy-vs-query drift. This closes the old scope gap from the bare focus triple: the blob carries group_id/root_uuid/match_scope/etc. AND the focus field. Reuses the shared navigator.clipboard->fallbackCopy idiom + showDockToast. Only meaningful for a cache-sourced SLICE render (dockedRenderSource==='slice'); in DOM mode it toasts guidance instead. One-shot (not a toggle).,
