  //   comment=THE single client-side fan-out for a server-echoed render_scope (Option Y, Dan's 'server is the one choke point' model). Called by displaySliceInDock on EVERY successful cache-projected render, regardless of which SURFACE triggered it (a Reader control -> usually a no-op adopt of the client's own values; an MCP glimpse(push_to_modal=true) call -> a real update that repaints the Reader chrome). It (1) stores the whole scope in dockedRenderScope (footer display source), (2) mirrors scope IDENTITY into dockedSliceContext (the re-render/per-row scope handle: group_id + root_uuid), and (3) mirrors the VIEW params (sort_by/sort_direction/since/headings_only) into the per-tab render state via setTabModalState so the Reader's View popover and chips repaint to match. Adoption is fail-closed for invalid server-echo `since`: the scope is decoded before any state mutation, and a malformed/string wire value surfaces through the yellow bar and aborts adoption, preserving last-known-good state. Otherwise the since field's existing draft guard (refreshSinceHeadingsUi skips overwriting sinceInput while it is focused) is preserved so a reply landing mid-type never stomps the user's keystrokes. Pure UI/state fan-out; no I/O, no server round-trip.,
