  //   comment=Display an Apply-slice server render in the dock as a standalone, cache-sourced, inherently-FROZEN document. Sets render PROVENANCE to 'slice' (+ dockedSliceContext={group_id,group_name} so a SLICE-mode Refresh re-applies the same slice), force-FREEZES (dockedRootUuid stays null -- a slice is NOT a DOM view, so live Workflowy clicks must not re-walk it), and POPULATES the top-half tree-view from the server's ordered rows (each carrying the (uuid, ancestor_path, occurrence) identity triple) instead of blanking it. Records the slice render mode -- 'snapshot' (server pre-rendered every row's option-Y view, kept in dockedSliceSnapshot keyed by sliceRowKey -> instant row clicks) or 'single' (large slice -> requestSliceRowRender on demand). Paints the full-document markdown (row 0's view) immediately, selects row 0 without re-rendering, and SUPPRESSES the scroll warning (cache_sourced; wired through selectionProvablyComplete). Sets dockedPaneHasGoodContent + the rendered source for char-count/Copy-MD.,
