  // @beacon[
  //   id=merge@request-merge-slice-groups,
  //   slice_labels=nexus--tags,slices,
  //   kind=ast,
  //   comment=THE wire helper for merge_slice_groups (the requestMutateNodeTags analog). Sends {action:'merge_slice_groups', request_id, endpoint_id, v:1, groups, mode, tag} with CANONICAL group refs (named = bare string; dynamic = {root_uuid, tags}) -- the Python _normalize_group_refs grammar, NOT the internal normalized refs. Timeout: args.timeout_seconds (an optional caller-declared wait deadline, e.g. set near a UI button) rides the frame as INTERIM transport metadata (NOT a spec field; REMOVED on the async-CARTO-job migration); fallback = conservative estimate (2.0 s x groups.length*20, 30 s floor; the true A8 value is server-side). Socket-drop settling rides failAllPendingSliceRenders. NO client-side persistence (A9): the server handler persists via create_slice_group; the reply carries the persistence record. NO UI affordance calls this in v1 (exactly how requestMutateNodeTags shipped).,
