  // deleted in this pass; do NOT reintroduce a local renderer here.
  //
  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // TRANSPORT/RENDER SEAM FIX (Opus 4.8 + Dan, 2026 — the root-cause fix).
  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // The mdTrace capture PROVED the spontaneous-wipe chain: a render request
  // (snapshot OR single) is in flight; the MV3 service-worker socket cycles
  // OPEN→CLOSED→OPEN (NORMAL — it does this constantly); the in-flight reply
  // is orphaned across the cycle and hits the 12s timeout → resolve(null);
  // by the time that STALE timeout fires, dockedRenderedGoodUuid has been
  // cleared by intervening activity, so the old per-uuid guard did NOT match,
  // and the pane was WIPED with 'server unavailable' — over content that was
  // rendering perfectly. (Observed: rid fired at gen=25 timing out at gen=29.)
  //
  // WebSocket unavailable policy: be stronger than you are. Say the simple truth.
  //
  // Show the WebSocket/broker-unavailable message only on cold start, when the
  // render pane is blank and there is no last-known-good document.
  //
  // After the first good server render, do NOT report later transport failures
  // in the render pane. Keep the last good document. A real outage then shows
  // up as "the modal does not update", not as an error painted over content.
  // This is intentional: repeated attempts to report every transient MV3 /
  // WebSocket failure produced false-positive wipes.
  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // @beacon[
  //   id=md-dock@render-selection-local,
  //   slice_labels=nexus--md-preview,
  //   kind=ast,
  //   comment=THE transport-failure sink for the docked modal (misnamed 'local' -- there is NO local composition since the server became the sole renderer). Rule: if dockedPaneHasGoodContent it is a pure no-op (last-known-good is sacred -- suppresses spontaneous MV3/WebSocket-blip wipes); only on a genuine COLD START (pane never rendered) does it paint the actionable 'GLIMPSE server unavailable' message. This is the DOM-path error sink the G2 unified-error-sink work must fold together with the slice/push failure modes. Beaconed for the async-render-correctness slice.,
